  "body": "With the introduction of HTTP/3, Fetch should likely have additions to the bad port list covering common UDP attack vectors.  As @davidben mentions in #1189 this should also probably explicitly apply to Alt-Svc and SVCB/HTTPS RR port targets.  For example, @mnot raised on the HTTP & QUIC WG this list:\r\n\r\n* 53 - DNS  (already a \"bad port\")\r\n* 123 - NTP  (already a \"bad port\")\r\n* 1900 - SSDP\r\n* 5353 - mDNS\r\n* 11211 - memcached\r\n\r\nThe alternative may be to switch to a \"good port\" list (#1189)",
